{
  "id": "nang_talung",
  "name": "Nang talung (southern Thai shadow-puppet theatre music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Shadow-puppet theatre of southern Thailand, centred on Nakhon Si Thammarat, Phatthalung and Songkhla, in which a single puppeteer (nai nang) moves cut-leather puppets behind a lit screen and voices every character, alternating sung verse with comic spoken dialogue in the southern dialect. Its small ensemble shares instruments with nora: pi oboe, thap goblet drums, klong drum, mong gongs and ching, and some modern troupes add Western drum kit and keyboard. The pi nai card stands in for the pi, a hand-drum card for the thap, generic drum and gong cards for the klong and mong, and a generic cymbal card for the ching.",
  "recipe": "classic modern nang talung, art Music, southeast Asian branch. heightened speech stylized intonation, solo with instrumental accompaniment, tonal language syllable tone locked melody, single lead single track no stacking. pi nai, hand drum source unspecified, membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum, gong tamtam, credited cymbals. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
